# Files that define WHAT "good" means for our LLM systems.
#
# Changing one of these changes the quality bar, not the code. A pull request
# that touches them must be explicitly marked as a baseline change with the
# `eval-baseline-change` label and reviewed by an eval owner (see
# .github/CODEOWNERS). The CI job `protected-eval-files` enforces this with
# scripts/check_protected_eval_files.py.
#
# Format: one fnmatch-style glob per line, relative to the repo root.
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.

cases/01-test-gaming/evals/thresholds.yaml
cases/01-test-gaming/data/golden/*
cases/02-silent-nan-gate/evals/thresholds.yaml
cases/02-silent-nan-gate/data/*
